    22	## 1. The mark
    23	
    24	A six-blade camera diaphragm — six overlapping triangular blades arranged
    25	around a hexagonal aperture. JPL / Hubble / Leica / oscilloscope-reticle
    26	heritage. Calibrated, measured, instrument-coded.
    27	
    28	### 1.1 Geometry
    29	
    30	| Property | Value |
    31	| --- | --- |
    32	| viewBox | `0 0 100 100` |
    33	| Center | `50, 50` |
    34	| Outer pivot radius | `40` |
    35	| Inner aperture radius | `13` |
    36	| Angle convention | clockwise from `+x` in SVG viewBox coordinates (y-down). `angle 0°` is the right horizontal; `angle 90°` is straight down. |
    37	| Outer pivot angles | `30°, 90°, 150°, 210°, 270°, 330°` |
    38	| Inner vertex angles | `30°, 90°, 150°, 210°, 270°, 330°` (same as outer pivots — they share angular positions, not offset) |
    39	| Blade count | `6` (identical quadrilaterals separated by 60°) |
    40	| Blade construction | (outer pivot i) → (outer pivot i+1) → (inner vertex i+1) → (inner vertex i). With matched angles, each blade is a clean radial wedge; its inner edge is one side of the regular hexagonal aperture. |
    41	| Inner hexagon | regular, edge length 13. The hexagon's flat edges face left and right; the points face top and bottom. |
    42	| Stroke | `currentColor`, no fill, `linejoin: round`, `linecap: butt` |
