frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:634:    <dt>Ink matching</dt><dd>Pantone values above are screen approximations. Proof against printed swatches before a run; lime must read fluorescent-adjacent on navy (389 C, or 802 C if the printer stocks it).</dd>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:635:    <dt>Text</dt><dd>All SVG text converts to outlines before handoff. Type is Archivo Narrow SemiBold, Archivo, and JetBrains Mono per DESIGN.md §5 (MVP stack is production).</dd>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:636:    <dt>Minimums</dt><dd>Mark reproduction floor is 8 mm (§1.5). Embroidery: satin stitch, thread ≥ 0.8 mm, mark no smaller than 50 mm.</dd>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:638:    <dt>Garments</dt><dd>Heavyweight blanks only: 240 gsm tees, 400 gsm fleece. Natural / ecru for paper goods, blackout navy for glass goods. Vendor pick is decision D-03.</dd>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:639:    <dt>Refuse list</dt><dd>Transfers in full (§10): no gradients, no pills or circular die-cuts, no drop shadows or bevels on the mark, no rotation of the mark, no lime on light garments, no decorative traces.</dd>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:650:      <strong>Is merch a brand-mode surface?</strong> STK-02 (duo hex) ships only if yes.
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:651:      <p>DESIGN.md §1.3 sanctions duo for favicon, public site, press kit, social avatar, anniversary, and deck page one. Swag is public-facing like the press kit, so the working assumption is yes, for exactly one piece. If sanctioned, add merch to the §1.3 list in a DESIGN.md update.</p>
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:658:      <strong>Pick blanks and printer.</strong> Specs assume 240 gsm tees and 400 gsm fleece in natural and blackout navy.
frontend/public/brand/merch/lookbook.html:659:      <p>Pantone matching for ink and signal happens at proof stage with the chosen vendor.</p>
frontend/public/brand/merch/sidira-print-reading.svg:3:  <desc id="desc">Chest/back print for glass-dark garments (#0A1421 blackout navy). A settle-trace reading as a record: signal-lime trace with its 18%-opacity phosphor underdraw, labeled readings axis with the 0.70 decision threshold marked, settled numeral in mono tabular, honest specimen provenance. Two inks: signal lime (#C8FF3D) and paper (#F4EFE6). Never printed on light garments (lime requires the dark ground, §4.1). Convert text to outlines before production.</desc>
